      "id": "t40",
      "group": "admin",
      "title": "DECIDE: BarkFest Dog Spaw sponsorship — $1,750 offer on the table",
      "taskStatus": "wip",
      "orderStatus": "na",
      "artStatus": "na",
      "order": [],
      "art": [],
      "cost": 1750,
      "notes": "OFFER AS AT 12 Aug (Yoko, 8:27pm): $1,750. She acknowledged the pricing discrepancy Rob raised and explained it: the $1,500 booth figure in the original $2,000 package was already a DISCOUNTED sponsor price (list on the 25x10 is $1,715), whereas the $1,795 she later quoted was straight a-la-carte list with no sponsor discount — which is why the two never reconciled. 10x15 is not a stock size so she was estimating by square footage. She also confirmed ALL sponsors get 10 tickets regardless, so those are back in. HER CONSTRAINT, in her words: the Dog Spaw feature must raise $2,500 total to cover the venue. The rescue side has $350 secured, so at $1,750 from Paw Prints she needs one more small sponsor at $400 to close it. That is why $1,750 is roughly her floor on this feature — but she offered to create a different feature area if the budget needs to be lower. VALUE AT LIST: 10x15 booth $1,170 + 1/4 ad $275 + web ads $350 + 10 tickets $200 = $1,995, or $2,245 if the 1,000 Wag Bag inserts ($250) are still included. Either way $1,750 is now a genuine discount rather than a premium. VS STAYING PLAIN: 10x10 booth $695 (already paid) + $75 extra pipe-and-drape + $275 ad = $1,045, plus the $50 Top Dog listing already on the application. So the sponsorship is roughly $700 more IF the $695 credits — and $1,750 on top if it does not. That single question is the whole decision. THE $2,500 EXPLAINED: that is not the sponsorship price, it is the total the Dog Spaw FEATURE must raise across all its sponsors to cover venue cost. $1,750 from Paw Prints + $350 already secured from the rescue side + $400 from one more small sponsor = $2,500. Which is also why she held at $2,000 earlier — $2,000 + $350 left her $150 short. TWO VERSIONS ON OFFER (Yoko, 11 Aug): (a) be the Dog Spaw sponsor, sharing the feature with rescue groups running nail trims and brush-outs on the other side, separated by a pipe-and-drape divider; or (b) \"an entirely different sponsorship so you're exclusive to the area\" under our own name. Rob's read is Leanne will want \"Paw Prints Calm K9 Corner\" kept either way, which points to (b). CAUTION on (b): Yoko said we \"wouldn't necessarily need to be part of the dog spaw area, and we could put you in a different location if you prefer\" — optional, but the current spot is the one she described as the quietest and furthest from the Main Stage. For a calm-dog concept that location is worth more than the branding. Also, as our own feature her $2,500 Dog Spaw target would not apply to us — which could cut either way on price.",
      "questions": [
